<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/Soft.jpg" alt="Use of edges in a chicken study" width="450" height="557" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Soft, Hard, Scrambled Edges. 10x8, oil on linen panel. 2015.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This painting was done to practice edge-work and to serve as a study for a future painting.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The surface is a medium texture linen, less smooth than the portrait grades that I use, consequently I had to use more paint than usual. I applied most of the paint with a palette knife, then used one or two bristle brushes to work on the edges. &nbsp;Once I had the edges down I made a few adjustments and laid in the highlights.</p>